hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21396","Abu Uthman Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Aban ibn Sa'id ibn al-As narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, he said, I heard Ziyad ibn Damrah ibn Sa'd al-Sulami narrating to Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said, My father and my grandfather narrated to me, and they had witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in Dhuhr prayer then sat in the shade of a tree, then al-Aqra' ibn Habis and Uyaynah ibn Hisn ibn Badr stood to him seeking the blood of the Ashja'i Amir ibn al-Adbat, who was that day the chief of Qays, and al-Aqra' ibn Habis was defending Muhallim ibn Jaththamah for Khindif, and they disputed before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, You take the blood money, fifty in this journey of ours and fifty when we return, Uyaynah said, By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I will not leave him until I make his women taste of grief what he made my women taste, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Rather you take the blood money, and Uyaynah refused, then a man of Layth stood called Mukaytil, a short compact man, and said, O Prophet of Allah, I found no likeness for this slain one at the beginning of Islam except as sheep that came to water, so its first was shot and its last fled, set precedent today and change tomorrow, he said, Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hand then said, Rather you accept the blood money in this journey of ours, fifty, and fifty when we return, and he kept with the people until they accepted the blood money, he said, When they accepted the blood money, he said, They said, Where is your companion for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to seek forgiveness for him, then a dark tall man stood wearing a suit, having prepared for killing, until he sat before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when he sat the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him, What is your name, he said, I am Muhallim ibn Jaththamah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, O Allah, do not forgive Muhallim, O Allah, do not forgive Muhallim, three times, then he stood from before him wiping his tears with the edge of his cloak, and as for us among ourselves we say, He sought forgiveness for him, but he showed what he showed so people would leave one another."
